## Error Handling

**Domain exceptions → HTTP responses. No silent failures.**

```python
# ✅ CORRECT: Explicit error handling
async def handle_reserve_inventory(self, cmd: ReserveInventoryCommand) -> UUID:
    try:
        material = await self.repo.get_by_id(cmd.material_id)
        if not material:
            raise MaterialNotFoundError(cmd.material_id)
        
        material.reserve(cmd.quantity)  # May raise InsufficientStockError
        
        await self.repo.save(material)
        return material.id
    except DomainException as e:
        logger.warning("Reservation failed", extra={"error": str(e)})
        raise  # Re-raise to be handled by exception middleware

# ❌ WRONG: Silent failure
try:
    material.reserve(quantity)
except:
    pass  # Silent — nobody knows what went wrong
```

